# The Eisenstein series E4 and the theta series of the eight-dimensional even unimodular lattice, which are the same
# function. A modular form of weight four is determined by one coefficient sequence, and for E4 that sequence is one
# followed by two hundred forty times the cube divisor sums: E4(q) = 1 + 240 sigma_3(1) q + 240 sigma_3(2) q^2 + ...
# The theta series of the eight-dimensional lattice counts vectors by squared length: theta(q) = sum over lattice points
# of q to the half squared length, and because that lattice is even and unimodular in dimension eight its theta series is
# a weight four modular form with constant term one, so it MUST equal E4. The consequence is exact and countable: the
# number of lattice vectors of squared length two n is two hundred forty times sigma_3(n). The n equals one shell is the
# kissing number two hundred forty, the n equals two shell is two thousand one hundred sixty, the n equals three shell is
# six thousand seven hundred twenty, the n equals four shell is seventeen thousand five hundred twenty. Each is a divisor
# cube sum scaled by two hundred forty, so the deepest counting fact about the densest eight-dimensional packing is a
# statement about modular forms, and it is checked here shell by shell against the cube divisor sums.

# Shell one, squared length two: 240 * sigma_3(1) = 240 * 1 = 240, the kissing number.
hold theta-shell-one-is-two-hundred-forty
  call is-equal
    code 240
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 1

# Shell two, squared length four: 240 * sigma_3(2) = 240 * 9 = 2160.
hold theta-shell-two-is-two-thousand-one-hundred-sixty
  call is-equal
    code 2160
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 9

# Shell three, squared length six: 240 * sigma_3(3) = 240 * 28 = 6720.
hold theta-shell-three-is-six-thousand-seven-hundred-twenty
  call is-equal
    code 6720
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 28

# Shell four, squared length eight: 240 * sigma_3(4) = 240 * 73 = 17520.
hold theta-shell-four-is-seventeen-thousand-five-hundred-twenty
  call is-equal
    code 17520
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 73

# The E4 lead coefficient is two hundred forty itself, the same two hundred forty that splits as one hundred twelve plus
# one hundred twenty-eight in the two root families. The theta series and the Eisenstein series agree at first order.
hold eisenstein-lead-coefficient-splits-as-the-two-root-families
  call is-equal
    code 240
    call add
      code 112
      code 128
